#: ../../../advanced/folder-filesystem-type.rst:2
msgid "filesystemType"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-filesystem-type.rst:4
msgid ""
"Syncthing has an internal abstraction for file system access with different "
"available implementations.  They can be configured per folder, with the "
"following possible values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-filesystem-type.rst:8
msgid "``basic`` (default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-filesystem-type.rst:9
msgid ""
"To be used if the folder is intended to store real data. Do not change "
"unless you are a developer and want to test things."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-filesystem-type.rst:12
msgid "``fake``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-filesystem-type.rst:13
msgid ""
"A fake file system type to be used for testing, e.g. when you want to create "
"a folder with a :abbr:`TB (Terabyte)` or more of random files that can be "
"synced somewhere, or an infinitely large folder to sync files into."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-filesystem-type.rst:17
msgid ""
"It has pseudorandom properties, i.e. data read from one fakefs can be "
"written into another fakefs, read back, and it will look consistent, without "
"any real data actually being stored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-filesystem-type.rst:21
msgid "To create an empty file system, use"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-filesystem-type.rst:23
msgid ""
"<folder id=\"default\" path=\"whatever\" ...>\n"
"    <filesystemType>fake</filesystemType>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-filesystem-type.rst:28
msgid "You can also specify that it should be prefilled with files,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-filesystem-type.rst:30
msgid ""
"<folder id=\"default\" path=\"whatever?size=2000000\" ...>\n"
"    <filesystemType>fake</filesystemType>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-filesystem-type.rst:35
msgid ""
"which will create a file system filled with 2 :abbr:`TB (Terabyte)` of "
"random data that can be scanned and synced. The prefilled data is based on a "
"deterministic seed, so you can index it, restart Syncthing, and the index "
"will still be correct for all the stored data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-filesystem-type.rst:40
msgid ""
"Check the source of `fakefs.go <https://github.com/syncthing/syncthing/blob/"
"main/lib/fs/fakefs.go>`_ for more options and details."
msgstr ""
